// What the codex says about an amulet. The drawing itself is built in,
// or comes from a picture in images/amulets/ with the same name as the id.
{
	"id": "vulture",
	"name": "Vulture",
	"plural": "vultures",
	"meaning": "Vultures were sacred to Nekhbet (the Goddess of Upper Egypt) and to Mut (the mother Goddess of Thebes). The Egyptian vulture, white with a yellow face, is also one of the commonest hieroglyphs."
}
